X`Generic Adventure 551' is a cleaned up and enhanced version of the 
Xold classic text game `Adventure'. It is based on a version close to the
Xseriously non-portable (and buggy) version for Primes posted last spring. I 
Xhave done a fair job of cleaning it up, portabilizing it, and debugging, but
Xit is still Fortran spaghetti. For you with no Fortran compilers, this is the 
Xexcuse you need to get "f2c" working!!! It has worked on the IBM-PC, VMS, the 
XMIPS 120, the IBM RISCstation 600, the VAX/Ultrix, and a Prime. It will
Xhowever expose toy Fortran compilers as just that - toys. I would like to 
Xthank Larry Estep for finding some hidden bugs.
X
XFor those that have not experienced this, the very first text adventure game,
Xit is a romp through the darkest reaches of Colossal Cave in search of
Xriches. You will find evocative descriptions of the darker, more mysterious
Xplaces of the earth, and severely test your abilities to map the
Xcontortions of the cave. You will find some hard - and some deceptively
Xeasy - puzzles to solve.
X
X
XDoug McDonald
